1. THE EXPOSURE DIFFERENCE, READ NOT ASSUMED
   112MSDCF: 79 frames  ISO 500  t=1/60s  f/11  200mm  2026:05:07 21:07:44  ILCE-7CM2
   113MSDCF: 63 frames  ISO 500  t=1/30s  f/11  200mm  2026:05:07 21:09:00  ILCE-7CM2
   ISO identical: True.  exposure ratio t113/t112 = 2.0000 = +1.0000 stops
   MECHANISM: the stop is EXPOSURE TIME, not gain.
   CONSEQUENCE, stated before the scale is measured: gain g and read
   noise in DN are IDENTICAL, 113 collected 2x the photons, so after
   photometric rescaling by c=1/2 it is strictly QUIETER than 112 --
   var -> c^2 var with the model evaluated on unscaled DN.
   calibration: g = 1.14469 DN/e-, rn_e = 1.47 (M41's constants)

2. ROI SELECTION (a1b window-mean procedure, unchanged)
   plane 3514x2344  detail (1671, 1373, 512, 512)  flat (2747, 32, 512, 512)

3. GLOBAL REGISTRATION between the two captures
