6. PHOTOMETRIC SCALE (registered ordering: model on unscaled DN)
   detail: median112/median113 = 0.5095
   flat  : median112/median113 = 0.5082
   EXIF prediction c = t112/t113 = 0.5000; measured (detail) 0.5095; disagreement 1.90%
   CHECK: PASS (<=5%)
   flat ROI level: 112 105.1 DN -> model sd 7.846 DN
                   113 206.8 DN -> model sd 10.944 DN
   after scaling 113 by c=0.5095: its sd becomes 5.576 DN, i.e. 0.7107x 112's.
   That ratio being BELOW 1 is the registered prediction and is what a
   longer exposure at equal gain must do.  The two halves of this FRC
   are therefore NOT equal-noise, which FRC tolerates (it is a
   normalised correlation) but which is stated rather than hidden.

